## CONTENTION BARRIER CANARY LAW

Barrier routing is opt-in only. Ordinary jobs pay no rendezvous cost.

A valid barrier action must remain timing-only:
- entrant: `grants_execution_authority=false`, next `WAIT_FOR_RELEASE_OR_TIMEOUT`;
- RELEASE: `grants_execution_authority=false`, next `RACE_DETERMINISTIC_PIN`;
- timeout: `pin_attempted=false`, next `REENTER_ALLOCATION`.

Before RELEASE, no portfolio PIN attempt is allowed. After valid RELEASE, every released entrant races the exact same deterministic generation from `post_release_claim`; only the PIN winner may create the matching execution claim. Losers create no execution claim, persist normal collision evidence when possible, and re-enter allocation.

If deadline passes without valid RELEASE, no late PIN attempt is allowed. A fresh fixture/barrier generation is required for another canary.

